\DOC basic_rectype_net

\TYPE {basic_rectype_net : (int * conv) net ref}

\SYNOPSIS
Net of injectivity and distinctness properties for recursive type constructors.

\DESCRIBE
HOL Light maintains a net used to simplify equations between elements of
recursive datatypes; essentially it contains the injectivity and distinctness
properties, e.g. {CONS_11} and {NOT_CONS_NIL} for lists. The injectivity
theorems are included as rewrites, but since there can be quadratically many
distinctness clauses, distinctness is handled instead by one conversion for
each constructor, which proves that it differs from all the other
constructors of its type (see {constructors_distinct_convs}). This net is used
in some situations where such things need to be proved automatically, notably
in {define}. The net itself is {!basic_rectype_net}. It is automatically
updated whenever a type is defined by {define_type}.

\FAILURE
Never fails.

\SEEALSO
cases, CONSTRUCTORS_DISTINCT_CONV, constructors_distinct_convs,
constructors_distinct_net, define, distinctness, extend_rectype_net,
GEN_BETA_CONV, injectivity.

\ENDDOC
